What is a BSPD?
  -A BSPD is a safety component that monitors the breaks
    -Prevents the driver from breaking and accelerating at the same time
  -If a break pressure value and a acceleration from the pedal are sent into the BSPD at the same time, the BSPD should trigger
  -Must use an op-amp to compare and scale voltages
    -Maybe LMH6611?
      -Can take min 2.7V and max 11V
      -In range of low voltage
      -Pin 5 allows for a shutdown of the op-amp for conserving power
        -Could maybe be useful?
